        "original_id": "3984ec52-a69c-598a-870c-42b69278b49b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jonny Craig, Pete Doherty\n- Bands and musical projects: Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, westerHALTS, the Libertines, Babyshambles, Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres\n- Albums and songs: The Greatest of All Lost Arts, “Pueblo Cicada”, “Last of the English Roses”\n\nFacts:\n- Jonny Craig was born on March 26, 1986, and he is a Canadian-American singer and songwriter.\n- In 1997, Pete Doherty formed the Libertines with Carl Barât and became its co-frontman.\n- Jonny Craig has been the lead vocalist for Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, and westerHALTS.\n- Pete Doherty is also associated with the musical projects Babyshambles and Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres.\n- Jonny Craig provided guest vocals on the song “Pueblo Cicada” from the 11-track album The Greatest of All Lost Arts.\n- “Last of the English Roses” is Peter Doherty’s debut solo single.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
